PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- Consensus remains unanimous on Choice B across all participants.
- The single-cell nested RT-PCR amplifies any intact B cell sequence-independently; thus, blank wells reflect physical absence of B cells caused by hydrodynamic shear dissociation of unstable, non-specific doublets between cuvette imaging and droplet pinch-off.
- The 4.2% recovery rate directly aligns with the natural precursor frequency of genuine, shear-resistant antigen-specific clones in an unselected repertoire.
- Competing options are definitively excluded due to factual contradictions (C), incorrect receptor terminology (D), biochemical impossibility (E), or incomplete mechanistic scope (A).
}

